      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "MicroPET in cynomolgus macaques showed that a fluoroethoxyphenyl-containing radiotracer crossed the BBB with high initial brain uptake, supporting CNS access for the query's OCH2CH2F aryl ether feature.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "Multiple high-transfer in vivo PET and biodistribution studies in rats, mice, and non-human primates consistently demonstrate BBB crossing and good brain uptake for closely related benzoxazole-stilbene and fluoroethoxyphenyl radiotracers. The query shares the key CNS-penetrant scaffold and substituent patterns, so meaningful CNS access is predicted.",
